              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "axios: Axios: Denial of Service via unbounded stream consumption when 'responseType: 'stream'' is used"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Axios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, when responseType: 'stream' is used, Axios returns the response stream without enforcing maxContentLength. This bypasses configured response-size limits and allows unbounded downstream consumption. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1."
